# .graphifyignore — Exclusions and contextual notes for the knowledge graph build
#
# This file is read by `graphify detect` and merged with .gitignore. Patterns
# follow gitignore syntax. Lines starting with # are comments.

# Legacy Node.js server — replaced by server_rust. Excluded from extraction
# so the knowledge graph reflects the current architecture only.
/src/

# Reverse-engineering sniffers — debug-only tools, not part of the production
# data path. They are still indexed by the graph (so the RE work shows up as
# context), but semantic extraction should treat their output as ephemeral
# debug traffic rather than production wiring. See .opencode/AGENTS.md for
# the operational policy: monitor.js is a RE bridge between Studio Manager
# and the physical mixer, used to capture SysEx round-trips for protocol
# discovery. It MUST NOT be treated as part of the production MIDI path.
#
# We don't exclude the file from detect (so the node exists in the graph),
# but flag it via the rationale attribute during semantic extraction.
# The semantic agent should add: rationale="debug-only RE sniffer, not
# part of the production data path; captures SysEx between Studio Manager
# and 01V96 for protocol reverse-engineering"
